Firstly answer to the topic: I wanted it to look a bit more unique and
not just YAFAP :P. I cannot remember all the details about my game for
I even got bored to Nethack for a while before managing to wrap this
up. Anyway, here are the mainparts:

I started this character mainly as a joke, Orly was a funny name
(http://www.orlytheowl.com and all). But as I ventured further I found
out that this was actually a good character and the first serious
caveman I had EVER played. I mean, the first that got further than dlvl
8. That is why I made a typical mistake and got expert at club and
sling and had no idea about the quest artifact mace. I ended up using
blessed +6 sling and blessed fireproof +7 club.

Although the damage I caused was quite minimal I survived all the way
to the castle where I gladly got displacement, MR and reflection
through GDSM, cloak of discplacement and The Shield of Reflection
(Perseus' statue didn't have one). After that I went to complete the
quest.

Gehennom was boring as usual; nothing to say about that.

Before going to meet Rodney I wanted more holy water and ended up
quaffing from a sink to make it become a fountain to dip potions at.
This was the worst mistake I did in the game; I polymorphed into a Gray
Dragon! I lost my cloak of displacement BUT luckily this way my armor
was saved. The rest of the game I went on with a blessed +0 leather
cloak...

After killing Rodney a couple of time I made it to planes using my +0
burnt speed boots which I had found in the later game. I had enchanted
my boots of jumping to +4 because I knew they would be in need on
Astral Plane. On the plane of Air Rodney summoned monsters everywhere
and I already thought I was about to die; luckily I had found five
wands of death and dealt with Rodney like that.

On Astral Plane I switched to the jumping boots and started
co-operating with my guardian angel and took the left altar first, I
encountered Death on the way and after slaying him once  boulder
blocked the way to the altar so I had enough time to recharge after
noticing it was chaotic.

Next I took the middle one (naturally)  and mostly jumped through
hostiles if Pestilence and Death got close. Finally made it on the
altar, just to notice that it was neutral.

On my way to the eastern altar my guardian angel got killed and that
was a real shame. I didn't have time to remember him so I continued
jumping and killed Famine on my way once. Unfortunately my way was
blocked and Famine got close to my few steps later. There it (or he?)
got me fainting and I died. No problem; my personal challenge was
broken. I had an Amulet of Life Saving. I put another one on and pushed
through towards the altar which happened to be, surprise surprise,
lawful!

You offer the amulet of Yendor to Anu... An invisible choir sings and
you are bathed in radiance... The voice of Anu rings out:
"Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of immortality!" You
ascend to the status of Demigod...

